{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a domain plugin that owns a ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slice, fetches a Swidux-defined JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a — same input always produces the same bucket, no network round-trip per read. Local overrides give QA a one-action toggle that wins over remote evaluation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes you have a Swidux app already wired up — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You also need somewhere to host a JSON file. Any URL works — Cloudflare Pages, R2, S3, a Worker, your own backend. The plugin doesn’t care.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxFeatureFlags\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 2: Add a state slice and action case","anchor":"Step-2-Add-a-state-slice-and-action-case"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SwiduxFeatureFlags","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var featureFlags: FeatureFlagsState = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case featureFlags(FeatureFlagsAction)","    \/\/ ... your other cases","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Hydrate state and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-3-Hydrate-state-and-register-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At app launch, hydrate state from your ","type":"text"},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (so the install ID and last-known-good config survive cold launches), then register the plugin:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let kv = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore()","let initial = AppState(","    featureFlags: .hydrated(from: kv)",")","","let store = Store(initialState: initial, reducer: AppReducer())","","let flags = FeatureFlagsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.featureFlags,","    action: AppAction.featureFlags,","    extractAction: { if case .featureFlags(let a) = $0 { return a } else { return nil } },","    service: HTTPFeatureFlagsService(url: configURL),","    keyValueStore: kv",")","store.register(plugin: flags)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Declare typed flag keys","anchor":"Step-4-Declare-typed-flag-keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare each flag once on a namespace so reads are type-safe:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["extension BoolFlag {","    static let newOnboarding = BoolFlag(\"new_onboarding\")","}","","enum CheckoutVariant: String { case control, treatment }","","extension VariantFlag where Variant == CheckoutVariant {","    static let checkoutLayout = VariantFlag(\"checkout_layout\", default: .control)","}","","extension ValueFlag where Value == Int {","    static let maxFreeUploads = ValueFlag(\"max_free_uploads\", default: 5)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 5: Read flags from views","anchor":"Step-5-Read-flags-from-views"},{"code":["if store.featureFlags.isEnabled(.newOnboarding) {","    NewOnboardingView()","}","","let layout = store.featureFlags.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","let cap = store.featureFlags.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 6: Refresh on foreground","anchor":"Step-6-Refresh-on-foreground"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin debounces ","type":"text"},{"code":".refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the configured ","type":"text"},{"code":"RefreshPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so it’s safe to dispatch on every ","type":"text"},{"code":"scenePhase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transition:","type":"text"}]},{"code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .active { store.send(.featureFlags(.refresh)) }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For wire format, bucketing, and exposure tracking details, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Add Feature Flags","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","title":"Add a Paywall","type